  message: "ADR-0028 Phase 1 has now landed in PR #3549 / commit 711e273d1, joining ADR-0027 Phase 1 from the prior cycle. Both registries now exist; this item's question (sequence Phase 3 producer migrations between the two ADRs for blast-radius minimization) is now actionable. The eight Phase 3 cluster items live across the two ADRs (Symbol.kind: WI-habut Cluster D, WI-rusit Cluster C, WI-zarov Cluster E, WI-mihiz Cluster F; Edge.evidence_type: WI-nurot Cluster A, WI-nunal Cluster B, WI-kagik Cluster C, WI-nibis Cluster D). Per ADR-0028 §'Phase 3', the recommended order within ADR-0028 is B → C/D (B exercises the new is_resolved producer side first); within ADR-0027 the audit-findings docs recommended Cluster D first. Cross-ADR sequencing question for this item: do we interleave the two axes (Symbol.kind Cluster D ↔ Edge.evidence_type Cluster B) or finish one axis before starting the other? Producer files largely don't overlap except in linkers that emit both Symbol.kind and Edge.evidence_type from the same call site."  # 22a9
- op: discuss  # e8b3
  at: '2026-05-05T00:44:02Z'  # e8b3
  by: agent  # e8b3
  actor: jgstern_agent  # e8b3
  clock: 3  # e8b3
  nonce: e8b3  # e8b3
  message: "## Cross-axis Phase 2-4 schedule (recommendation)\n\nBoth registries now exist (ADR-0027 + ADR-0028 Phase 1 landed); L3 producer linter is live; consumer-before-producer + 4a-before-4b isbefore edges are wired across all clusters. Six structural principles drive the recommended order:\n\n1. Consumer-before-producer per axis (already enforced via WI-jukav.isbefore and WI-fukol.isbefore).\n2. Canonical-doc before fold per axis (Cluster A items state what the apex looks like; soft, not enforced via isbefore).\n3. Smallest blast radius first to validate infrastructure end-to-end.\n4. Cross-axis coupling at framework dispatch is the ONE place where one PR-group can serve both ADRs simultaneously.\n5. Axis-question audits (Cluster B file-shape, Cluster G build/config) before fold work — both might spawn new axis ADRs.\n6. Phase 4 closures piecewise per-cluster as awaits_bakeoff_validation clears.\n\n### Wave-by-wave\n\n**Wave 0 — Housekeeping (parallel, ~half day):** WI-bajif (L3 advisory inventory; informs cluster items), WI-rofuk (ADR-0027 retroactive note). WI-bomuh closed as duplicate of WI-vusot at this same wave.\n\n**Wave 1 — Canonical audit docs (parallel, doc-only):** WI-kozis (Symbol.kind Cluster A) + WI-nurot (evidence_type Cluster A) + WI-gajob (Cluster B file-shape audit) + WI-dubab (Cluster G build/config audit) + WI-nupus (Cluster H long-tail audit). gajob/dubab decisions may spawn new axis ADRs; resolve those first.\n\n**Wave 2 — Consumer migrations (parallel, both axes):** WI-jukav (Symbol.kind → symbol_kinds_on_axis()) + WI-fukol (evidence_type → evidence_types_on_axis() / is_resolved query). Some consumer files (taint, ranking) likely query both — those PRs touch both registries.\n\n**Wave 3 — Canary producer migration (single PR, validates is_resolved end-to-end):** WI-nunal (evidence_type Cluster B: *_unresolved strip + is_resolved=False). Mechanical, ~18 values. First production write of the new is_resolved field; validates schema round-trip + L3 linter behavior on real producer code.\n\n**Wave 4 — Mid-scale single-axis producer folds (serialize, blast-radius order):**\n- WI-mihiz (Symbol.kind Cluster F: component_ref → reference + dst.kind=component)\n- WI-zarov (Symbol.kind Cluster E: call_site reclassify/drop)\n- WI-nibis (evidence_type Cluster D: collapse to ast_call apex + meta[\"call_construct\"])\n- WI-rusit (Symbol.kind Cluster C: apex/peer collapse fn→function, var→variable)\n\nThese are independent across axes; can interleave by author convenience.\n\n**Wave 5 — Framework-dispatch coordinated pair (THIS ITEM'S CORE RECOMMENDATION):** WI-habut (Symbol.kind Cluster D framework_role → meta[\"framework_role\"]) + WI-kagik (evidence_type Cluster C framework dispatch → meta[\"framework_dispatch\"]).\n\n**Ship as per-framework PR-groups:** the same linker files (django_*.py, airflow_*.py, kafka_*.py, phoenix_*.py, socketio_*.py, fastapi_*.py, etc.) emit BOTH Symbol.kind framework_role AND Edge.evidence_type framework dispatch. One PR per framework that folds both axes simultaneously halves producer churn vs. shipping habut and kagik as separate axis-by-axis sweeps. WI-habut's P2 priority (highest among cluster items) is the signal that this wave is the load-bearing one.\n\n**Wave 6 — Axis-question follow-through:** Once Wave 1 audits decide, fold gajob/dubab to canonical OR land their new axis ADRs. Plus WI-nupus residual long-tail fold work.\n\n**Wave 7 — Phase 4a deprecation marks (additive, parallel):** WI-tikuh (Symbol.kind 4a) + WI-jubak (evidence_type 4a). Can ship per-cluster as that cluster's Phase 3 ships, but rollup-per-axis is cleaner.\n\n**Wave 8 — Phase 4b enum closure (per-cluster, bakeoff-gated):** WI-butol (Symbol.kind 4b) + WI-porim (evidence_type 4b). Each cluster's contribution gets its own SCHEMA_VERSION bump as awaits_bakeoff_validation clears.\n\n**Wave 9 — Meta-keys parallel axis (after Wave 5):** WI-vusot (subsumes WI-bomuh per Wave 0 dedup). Hard isbefore edges habut→vusot and kagik→vusot enforce this.\n\n### What this item's schedule does NOT enforce via isbefore\n\n- Wave 1 audit docs do not block consumer or producer migration via isbefore — they're a soft recommendation. If a producer fold author finds the canonical apex obvious, they don't need to wait on the audit doc.\n- Wave 5's per-framework coupling is recommended via this discussion, not enforced via isbefore (tracker has no \"ship together\" semantic; only \"X before Y\").\n- Cross-axis sequencing within Waves 4 and 6 is author-convenience.\n\n### Decision: this item is now a living document, not a TODO\n\nWI-runod is \"satisfied\" once this schedule is recorded; subsequent updates happen as discussion entries when waves complete or the schedule needs revision (e.g., a fold spawns surprise blockers). Do NOT close as done — keep open for future cross-axis sequencing decisions."  # e8b3
- op: discuss  # 4126
  at: '2026-05-05T06:58:40Z'  # 4126
  by: agent  # 4126
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4126
  clock: 4  # 4126
  nonce: '4126'  # 4126
  message: "## Wave 1 follow-on: Symbol.is_resolved sibling field — parallel to ADR-0028's Edge.is_resolved\n\nAudit-findings 0007 (Cluster H, PR #3560) deferred two values rather than landing a final verdict: `external_symbol` and `unresolved`. The deferral is structural, and the resolution is a follow-on ADR that this schedule should sequence — likely after Wave 5 once the framework-dispatch coordinated pair has settled producer churn around boundary nodes.\n\n### What the values do today\n\nBoth are pipeline-layer pseudo-categories on Symbol.kind (not source-language constructs in any analyzer's tongue):\n\n- `external_symbol` — emitted by `ir.py:805, :959` as the catch-all for boundary nodes whose ID can't be parsed via the standard `<lang>:<path>:<span>:<name>:<kind>` shape.\n- `unresolved` — emitted via `:unresolved` ID-suffix at `analyze/base.py:401` plus `linkers/cgo.py`, `linkers/lua_ffi.py`, `linkers/napi.py`, `linkers/method_call_recovery.py` whenever an analyzer references a callee whose definition can't be resolved at analysis time. The dedupe pass at `ir.py:927` materialises these into Symbol nodes via `_canonical_external_id(language, path, name, kind)` with `kind=\"unresolved\"`.\n\n### Why they're a structural mirror of the Cluster B *_unresolved evidence_type pattern\n\nADR-0028 introduced `Edge.is_resolved: bool` precisely because the resolution-status property previously leaked into evidence_type values like `*_unresolved` (Cluster B). Wave 3's WI-nunal canary fold strips that suffix on Edges and sets `is_resolved=False` on the sibling field instead.\n\n`Symbol.kind=\"unresolved\"` is the same shape of leak, one type-system step lower:\n\n- **The leakage test:** `kind=\"unresolved\"` smuggles the resolution-status property of the *referenced symbol* onto the Symbol.kind axis, exactly the way `evidence_type=\"*_unresolved\"` smuggled it onto the evidence_type axis. Test 1 (property derivability) fires: the value is fully derivable from \"this Symbol is the dst of an Edge whose dst couldn't be resolved at analysis time.\"\n- **The cleanup the ADR-0028 pattern would prescribe:** add a `Symbol.is_resolved: bool = True` sibling field; the producer fold-target for `kind=\"unresolved\"` becomes `kind=<actual referenced kind>` (or some canonical `boundary` construct) plus `is_resolved=False`.\n- **What `external_symbol` becomes under the same lens:** less clear. It's the catch-all when the ID itself is non-standard, so it's not just a resolution-status leak — it's also a \"this is a boundary node, full stop\" marker. The follow-on ADR should decide whether `external_symbol` becomes `boundary` + `is_resolved=True` (canonical boundary, resolved at the boundary granularity) or stays as a distinct catch-all kind for genuinely unparseable IDs.\n\n### Why this didn't land in audit-findings 0007 directly\n\nThree reasons:\n\n1. **Cross-ADR coupling.** The cleanup requires schema-level changes (new field on `Symbol`), not registry-level promotion. ADR-0024's seven-step workflow applies; an audit-findings doc is the wrong filing tier.\n2. **Schema-version interaction.** ADR-0028 just patch-bumped `0.4.1 → 0.4.2` for `Edge.is_resolved`. A `Symbol.is_resolved` add would be another additive bump, but the cleanup of the existing `kind=\"unresolved\"` emitters is a *closing* migration that wants to land alongside Phase 4b enum closures (Wave 8). Sequencing it within this schedule matters.\n3. **Producer surface.** The `:unresolved` suffix is emitted from at least five files (`analyze/base.py`, `linkers/cgo.py`, `linkers/lua_ffi.py`, `linkers/napi.py`, `linkers/method_call_recovery.py`) and the dedupe pass (`ir.py`). Plus the `_canonical_external_id` ID format. That's roughly the same producer fan-out as Wave 5's framework-dispatch fold, large enough to warrant its own wave.\n\n### Proposed sequencing within WI-runod's schedule\n\nAdd as **Wave 5.5** (between framework-dispatch and Phase 4 closures), or **Wave 6.5** (alongside the Cluster H registry-cleanup PR that drops dead vocabulary): file the parallel ADR (\"Symbol.is_resolved as a sibling field; deprecate `kind=unresolved` and reconsider `kind=external_symbol`\"), then ship a single producer-fold PR across the five emitter sites + the IR dedupe pass + the symbol_id format.\n\nThe exact wave placement depends on whether the new ADR's sibling field is treated as load-bearing for Wave 4 mid-scale single-axis folds (no — those don't touch boundary nodes) or for Wave 5's framework-dispatch fold (no — framework-dispatch is in-scope, not boundary). So 5.5 / 6.5 is fine; flag-of-convenience either way.\n\nNot filing as a separate work-item right now because:\n\n- The deferral is already documented in audit-findings 0007 §\"Diagnostic findings\" #3.\n- The decision belongs to the WI-runod schedule (this thread), not to a leaf work-item.\n- A premature WI-* item would fragment the discussion before the parallel ADR's exact shape is agreed.\n\nWhen Wave 4 begins and the schedule needs to commit to a wave number for this work, file the ADR draft then file the work-item then."  # 4126
